    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="ec414efe-1d79-5b6a-bfd9-69c514aeed08" activityNameId="ae613249-4b7e-57ea-b764-ff603eedb5de" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Sewer system, construction, reinforced concrete pipe, DN 300, profile 2</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Sewer system, construction, reinforced concrete pipe, DN 300, profile 2
Modern Swiss und European technologies are applied to building machines, material production and building processes. 
UUID: 2c7256f8-8103-4c28-b8c2-a1a079b2feb9
This process models 1 meter of installed sewer infrastructure with reinforced concrete pipe and a trench depth of 3 meters. This process includes the production phase (A1–A3) and the construction phase/ transport (A4–A5) for 1 meter of installed reinforced concrete pipe, including trench excavation and backfilling. Disposal and deconstruction processes are excluded and modelled separately specific for each sewer system type. The operation of similar types of building machines across different processes is aggregated to one process.
Location: Switzerland
Technology: DN 300, profile 2 according to SIA 190.Trench depth 3 meters. Reinforced concrete pipe, ID 300 mm, outer diameter 440 mm, wall thickness 70 mm, 225 kg/m, 2770 kg/m³
Time period: Review of data currency scheduled after 5 years.
Production volume: 
Sampling: 
Extrapolations: None
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_2c7256f8-8103-4c28-b8c2-a1a079b2feb9.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
